<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11353" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cōrycĭus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κωρύκιος</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>Corycian</i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Of</i> or <i>belonging to the Corycian
				mountain cave</i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κωρύκιον
			ἄντρον</span>) <i>on Parnassus, famous in ancient
				fable</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Co rycium nemus,</span>”
				i. e. <i>Parnassian</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					Th. 7, 347</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">umbra,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. S.
					5, 3, 5</span></i>
			.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cōrycĭdes</span></b> 
			Nymphae, <i>the daughters of
			Plistus</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 1, 320</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Of</i> or <i>pertaining to the
				promontory Corycus;</i> v. 2. Corycus, II.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
